-- title:
--   Affine probability parameters commute with pushforward
-- statement:
--   For finite sets $V,W$, a map $f:V\to W$, parameters $c:W\to[0,1]$, and a probability distribution $p$ on $V$, define $\lambda_c(q)=\sum_w q(w)c(w)$. Then
--   $$\lambda_c(f_*p)=\lambda_{c\circ f}(p).$$
--   Thus the affine parameter can be computed before or after pushing the distribution forward.
-- source:
--   Ruijun Wang, Continuous graph homomorphisms of higher dimensional abelian group actions, arXiv:2609.39824v1 (2026), Sections 3–6 and Proposition 7.1; https://arxiv.org/html/2609.39824v1. This helper is formalization-specific infrastructure, not a separately numbered assertion of the paper. Original Lean proof: AbelianTargets/SupportChartNaturality.lean, lines 15–27; raw UTF-8 source SHA-256 9b07eeb4faaa5e016de3c47ce1afbf496e48bd8dc4f27ec01a8dce8d0409d56a. No public source repository commit was available.

